    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule itself is present in the visible records; the decision relies on a structurally related morphinan (samidorphan) and the physicochemical prior.",
    "Samidorphan differs from the query in N-substituent and aromatic substituents, which could affect metabolism and absorption.",
    "The L4 records are for unrelated molecules and formulations; no query-specific intestinal absorption, solubility, or permeability data are available.",
    "No formulation-specific, dose-ranging, or condition-matched data for the query are available in the visible records."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Keep high (F >= 20%): the query is an oxycodone-type 4,5-epoxymorphinan-6-one with a favorable physicochemical prior, and the closest visible measured analog samidorphan has an absolute oral bioavailability of about 69%. The L4 dissolution/solubility records are for unrelated molecules and do not change the decision; no visible record provides affirmative evidence for F < 20%. Confidence remains moderate because the strongest evidence comes from a structural analog rather than a direct query measurement."
}

